 # Dashboard Layout Patterns

## Pattern Recognition Guide

When analyzing dashboard designs, look for these common layout structures:

### 1. Analytics Grid (4-4-4)
```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6">
  {/* Top row stats */}
  <div className="col-span-4">
    <StatCard />
  </div>
  <div className="col-span-4">
    <StatCard />
  </div>
  <div className="col-span-4">
    <StatCard />
  </div>
</div>
```

### 2. Main-Sidebar (9-3)
```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6">
  {/* Main content area */}
  <div className="col-span-9">
    <div className="space-y-6">
      {/* Content sections */}
    </div>
  </div>
  {/* Sidebar */}
  <div className="col-span-3">
    <div className="space-y-6">
      {/* Sidebar widgets */}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

### 3. Dashboard Card Patterns

#### Full-Width Chart Card
```tsx
<div className="rounded-lg border bg-card p-6">
  <div className="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
    <div className="space-y-1">
      <h3 className="font-semibold">Chart Title</h3>
      <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Subtitle</p>
    </div>
    <div className="flex items-center gap-4">
      <DateRangePicker />
      <FilterDropdown />
    </div>
  </div>
  <div className="h-[400px]">
    <ChartComponent />
  </div>
</div>
```

#### Split Chart Card
```tsx
<div className="rounded-lg border bg-card p-6">
  <div className="grid grid-cols-2 gap-8">
    <div className="space-y-4">
      <div className="aspect-square">
        <ChartComponent />
      </div>
    </div>
    <div className="space-y-4">
      <div className="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        {stats.map(stat => (
          <StatItem key={stat.id} {...stat} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

### 4. Common Dashboard Sections

#### Header Section
```tsx
<div className="flex items-center justify-between mb-6">
  <div className="space-y-1">
    <h1 className="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Dashboard</h1>
    <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Your analytics overview
    </p>
  </div>
  <div className="flex items-center gap-4">
    <DateRangePicker />
    <Button>Export</Button>
  </div>
</div>
```

#### Stats Overview
```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
  {stats.map(stat => (
    <div key={stat.id} className="rounded-lg border bg-card p-6">
      <div className="flex items-center gap-4">
        <stat.icon className="h-5 w-5 text-muted-foreground" />
        <div className="space-y-1">
          <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{stat.label}</p>
          <p className="text-2xl font-semibold">{stat.value}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div className="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <TrendIndicator value={stat.trend} />
        <span className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          vs previous period
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  ))}
</div>
```

### 5. Responsive Considerations

#### Mobile-First Breakpoints
```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
  {/* Cards that stack on mobile, 2-up on tablet, 3-up on desktop, 4-up on large screens */}
</div>
```

#### Responsive Navigation
```tsx
<div className="hidden lg:flex flex-col gap-2">
  {/* Desktop sidebar navigation */}
</div>
<div className="lg:hidden">
  <MobileNav /> {/* Mobile navigation menu */}
</div>
```

### Pattern Recognition Steps

1. **Identify Major Sections**
   - Look for clear visual divisions
   - Note content hierarchy
   - Identify repeated patterns

2. **Analyze Grid Structure**
   - Count columns in each section
   - Note responsive behavior
   - Identify nested grids

3. **Component Patterns**
   - Look for repeated card styles
   - Note consistent spacing
   - Identify common UI patterns

4. **Spacing Patterns**
   - Note gaps between sections
   - Look for consistent padding
   - Identify margin patterns

5. **Interactive Elements**
   - Note hover states
   - Identify click targets
   - Look for loading states

Remember: When implementing these patterns, always consider the content hierarchy and user flow. The layout should enhance the user experience, not hinder it.